{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeLSQVodPeiZHkanG7r8h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Verdict\n\n`approve with required changes`. The plan's product interpretation, type surface, and ownership split are sound and match the repository (`app/` has only `page.tsx`/`layout.tsx`/`globals.css`, so a nested `app/trade-capture/` route is genuinely isolated). But three classes of defect would break the run as written: the lifecycle contract cannot preserve a trade's identity or audit history across edit/book/cancel, the domain test as specified (`node --test tests/trade-domain.test.ts`) is incompatible with this repo's `tsconfig.json` and Node ESM resolution, and three of four workers cannot compile from one baseline because their imports do not yet exist.\n\n## Required contract changes\n\n1. **Lifecycle functions, not just `materializeTrade`.** `materializeTrade(draft, {id,status,at})` (ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md:171) has no way to carry prior `auditEvents`, so re-booking an edited trade silently discards history — the product requires cancellation \"while preserving its history\" (PRODUCT.md:27). Freeze in `domain/lifecycle.ts` (Terra-owned): `saveDraft(existing: Trade | null, draft, ctx): Trade`, `validateTradeRecord(existing, draft, ctx): Trade`, `bookTrade(existing, draft, ctx): Trade`, `cancelTrade(trade, ctx): Trade`. Each preserves `internalTradeId` and appends to `auditEvents`; `bookTrade` throws if `validateTrade` returns any `severity: \"error\"`; `cancelTrade` throws unless `status === \"booked\"`. Add `\"updated\"` to `AuditEvent.action`.\n2. **Add `editingTradeId: string | null` to reducer state** (the state list at ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md:46 omits it). Define: `onEditDraft(id)` loads that trade into the ticket and sets `editingTradeId`; save/validate/book target that ID when set, otherwise mint a new one; `onReset` clears it; cancelled trades are not editable.\n3. **Pin `signedExposure` and every `DeskSummary` field.** Currently undefined whether exposure is current face or gross principal, and whether `sellExposure` is negative. Freeze: `signedExposure = side === \"buy\" ? grossPrincipal : -grossPrincipal`; `buyExposure` = sum of positive `signedExposure`; `sellExposure` = sum of negative `signedExposure` (negative number); `netExposure = buyExposure + sellExposure`; `grossPrincipal` = sum of `Math.abs(signedExposure)`; `activeTradeCount` = trades with status ≠ `cancelled`; `bookedTradeCount` = status `booked`; `exceptionCount` = `error`-severity exceptions on non-cancelled trades. Without this, Terra computes and Qwen renders different quantities.\n4. **Move the domain test to `tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`.** `tsconfig.json:5` sets `\"types\": [\"@cloudflare/workers-types\"]`, so `@types/node` is not in the program while `include` (tsconfig.json:26-33) covers `**/*.ts`; a `.ts` test importing `node:test`/`node:assert` will fail `npm run typecheck`. `.mjs` files are outside `include`, matching every existing test (`tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`, `benchmark/fixtures/**/*.test.mjs`).\n5. **Fix TS import resolution for that test.** Node runs `.ts` by type stripping (env records `node v26.0.0`), but ESM requires explicit extensions: all relative imports inside `app/trade-capture/domain/` and from the test must be `./types.ts` style, and all type-only imports must use `import type` (stripping cannot erase a value import of a type). This requires `\"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true` in `tsconfig.json`, which no worker owns. **Assign `tsconfig.json` to the Sol integrator and make the change in the frozen baseline, not during integration.**\n6. **Wire the domain test into `npm test` in the baseline.** `package.json:12` is `npm run build && node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`; `verify` (package.json:15) never runs the domain test. Change baseline `test` to `npm run build && node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`, otherwise Terra's work is ungraded by the gate.\n7. **Do not require `npm run build` in worker stages.** `app/layout.tsx:2` uses `next/font/google`, which fetches Geist on a cold cache; sandboxed workers with no network will fail a build they did not break. Worker commands: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and (Terra) the domain test only.\n8. **Make the reducer and blotter selection pure and importable.** Put `tradeCaptureReducer`, `TradeCaptureState`, and `selectVisibleTrades(trades, {product,status,search,sort})` in `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts` and `selectors.ts` with no React import, so filtering, sorting, selection, and cancellation are testable by `node --test` without a browser. As drafted, none of the required interactions have an objective check.\n9. **Freeze exception codes and field ids.** Terra publishes `export const EXCEPTION_CODES` (string literal union) and every `TradeException.field` must be an actual `TradeDraft` key (drop the redundant `| \"allocations\"`). Sonnet must render each control with `id={`tc-field-${field}`}`, `aria-invalid` when an error targets it, and `aria-describedby` pointing at `tc-error-${field}`. Assign cross-field rules to one owning field: settlement-before-trade → `settlementDate`; modifier/product conflicts → `modifier`; agency requirement → `agency`; allocation total → `allocations`.\n10. **State allocation-editing scope.** No component in the prop tables owns allocation entry, yet rule 11 and `AllocationInput` exist. Either give Sonnet an explicit add/remove allocation row group, or declare allocations read-only for the first mock (seed-supplied, shown in `TradeReview`, still validated). Pick one in the contract.\n11. **Cent comparison helper.** Export `withinOneCent(a, b)` implemented as `Math.abs(Math.round(a*100) - Math.round(b*100)) <= 1` from the domain and require Kimi and the seed to use it; \"within one cent\" plus raw float subtraction is where `0.1 + 0.2` bites.\n12. **Determinism rules for hydration.** `EMPTY_TRADE_DRAFT` must contain constant strings (no `new Date()` at module scope); `SEED_TRADES` timestamps must be hard-coded ISO strings; new IDs and `AuditEvent.at` may only be produced inside reducer action handling, never during render. Otherwise SSR and client output diverge and rendered assertions are unstable.\n13. **CSS isolation rule.** `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css` must contain no bare element selectors, no `:root`, and no `*` rules; every selector must begin with `.tc-`. It is loaded into the same global cascade as `app/globals.css` (which already sets `body`, `*`, `button`, `a`).\n14. **Accessibility floor, stated as contract.** Blotter is a `<table>` with `<caption>`; row selection is a real `<button>` inside a cell (not `onClick` on `<tr>`) with `aria-pressed`; the scroll container has `tabindex=\"0\"`, `role=\"region\"`, and an accessible name; validation summary is a `role=\"status\"` live region; Book uses `disabled` **plus** a visible reason. Accessibility failure is a blocking category, and this is split across two workers.\n\n## Domain review\n\nCalculations match PRODUCT.md:95-100, but `calculateEconomics` takes non-null numbers while every draft numeric is `number | null`; specify that the caller passes `0`-guarded values and that `validateTrade` alone reports blanks. Status transitions are described but unowned — item 1 fixes that. Validation ownership is correctly single-source (Terra) as long as Kimi is forbidden from re-deriving \"can book\"/\"can cancel\". Cancelled-trade totals are handled for exposure but not for `exceptionCount` (item 3). Seed rules: `SEED_TRADES: readonly Trade[]` lets hand-written `exceptions` drift from `validateTrade`; require seeds to be produced by the frozen lifecycle helpers at module init, and add a test asserting each seed's exceptions equal `validateTrade(seedDraft)`. Identifiers: the nine-character uppercase check should be `^[A-Z0-9]{9}$` applied after trimming and uppercasing, and TBA MBS still needs a security identifier — confirm that is intended. Synthetic-name rule (PRODUCT.md:145) needs an objective form: counterparties/books/traders must use `MOCK-`/desk-style labels, trade IDs prefixed `TCM-`.\n\n## Component and state review\n\nProps are coherent. Gaps: `TradeBlotterProps.trades` does not say whether it is the full or filtered list — specify full list plus filter state, with `selectVisibleTrades` applied inside. `TradeTicketProps.exceptions` does not say when they are recomputed — specify live recomputation on every draft change, with `onValidate` additionally setting status `validated` and appending an audit event; `onBook` re-validates before committing. `TradeReviewProps.onCancel` needs the guard in item 1 and a defined focus target after cancellation. Route isolation is otherwise fine: `worker/index.ts:43` passes everything to the app-router handler, so `/trade-capture` needs no worker change, and `app/page.tsx:1` is already `\"use client\"` and untouched. Only `trade-capture-app.tsx` should carry `\"use client\"`.\n\n## Worker isolation review\n\nThe plan asserts non-overlapping ownership but its sequence (ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md:268-275) contradicts the block rule that each stage runs in a fresh worktree from a committed baseline: Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi all import `domain/types.ts`, and Kimi imports Sonnet's and Qwen's components — none of which exist at the planning baseline `d911c5f`. As written, three workers cannot typecheck or lint their own output.\n\n**Corrected sequencing rule.** Sol commits baseline **B1** containing, as integrator-owned frozen files: `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts` (types only), `app/trade-capture/domain/index.ts` re-exports, `page.tsx`, the `tsconfig.json` and `package.json` changes, and compiling stubs for all five worker files (`throw new Error(\"not implemented\")` for domain functions; minimal semantic markup for the four components). Terra then owns `calculations.ts`, `validation.ts`, `lifecycle.ts`, `seed.ts`, and `tests/trade-domain.test.mjs` — **not** `types.ts`. Commit Terra's result as **B2**; run Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi in parallel from B2, each replacing exactly one owned file (Kimi replaces four). Every stage can then run `typecheck` and `lint` green, and any red is attributable.\n\n## Verification gaps\n\nAutomated, currently missing: reducer transitions (draft→validated→booked→cancelled, illegal transitions rejected); `selectVisibleTrades` filter/search/sort/tie-breaking; audit-history preservation across edit and cancel; seed exceptions equal `validateTrade` output; `summarizeDesk` excluding cancelled trades; a rendered assertion that `/trade-capture` returns 200 with the synthetic notice, blotter `<caption>`, `<label for=`, `aria-describedby`, and a `role=\"status\"` region, plus a negative assertion that `/` contains no `tc-` markup. Note `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:10` hard-codes `http://localhost/`; Sol must parameterize the path while keeping the existing assertions. Avoid asserting exact `Intl` currency strings — the built worker runs under Node in this test, and spacing can differ from workerd; assert on digits and labels.\n\nManual-only (later, browser): visible keyboard focus, tab order, 390-pixel layout without page-level horizontal overflow, focus movement after select/cancel, console errors, reload-resets-state, and live filter/sort interaction.\n\n## Optional improvements\n\n1. Sortable column headers with `aria-sort` instead of (or mirroring) the sort select, plus a visible \"showing N of M\" count and an empty-state row.\n2. Extend `scripts/benchmark-validate.mjs` to assert the T7 block's `product.sha256` and planning `prompt_sha256`, as the other blocks are checked (lines 119-139).\n3. Per-product settlement-convention hint text as an informational note, reinforcing PRODUCT.md:109-111 without adding a rule.\n4. A `formatting.ts` shared by Qwen and Kimi (`formatUsd`, `formatSignedUsd`, `formatFace`, `formatPercent`) to keep displayed money consistent across panels.\n5. `prefers-reduced-motion` handling and a print-friendly review panel for the ticket/blotter."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1638,"cache_read_input_tokens":52040,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1638},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64ac4aac-c683-4d8a-a5fd-3c35d9ba90ee","uuid":"a61deb9f-c67f-49ac-a7c1-92245d6b77bb","timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:06:25.238Z","request_id":"req_011CeLSQV2za1NzJKWnKAnFr"}
